            "content": [
              {
                "type": "output_text",
                "text": "I don’t have live web access, so I can’t verify the very latest Mars Perseverance rover news in real time. As of my reliable knowledge cutoff in **June 2024**, the key updates were:\n\n- **Perseverance was exploring Jezero Crater’s ancient river delta**, studying rocks that may preserve signs of past microbial life.\n- The rover had already collected and sealed many **rock-core samples** for possible future return to Earth through the Mars Sample Return campaign.\n- **Ingenuity**, the small helicopter that accompanied Perseverance, ended its mission in **January 2024** after damaging a rotor blade, but it far exceeded expectations with 72 flights.\n- Perseverance continued using its instruments—such as **SHERLOC, PIXL, SuperCam, and Mastcam-Z**—to analyze Martian geology and search for potentially habitable ancient environments.\n- NASA and ESA were reassessing the architecture and cost of the **Mars Sample Return** mission, which affects how and when Perseverance’s collected samples might eventually reach Earth.\n\nFor the newest updates, the best source is NASA’s Perseverance mission page or NASA/JPL news releases.",
